===============================================================================
SCOPE OF THE ABOVE, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER
===============================================================================

The MIT license above applies to the code, configuration, documentation and
measurement records in this repository.

It does NOT apply to the corpus-derived text files listed below. Those files
contain text taken from the OpenWebText corpus (Skylion007/openwebtext), which
is a collection of third-party web documents. They are not the authors' work
to license and are not relicensed here.

  bursts/context.txt          verbatim span of one OpenWebText document
                              (document index 73, 760 words)
  bursts/scrambled_corpus.txt window-shuffled span of one OpenWebText document
                              (document index 104, 485 words)
  bursts/pos_substituted.txt  part-of-speech-substituted span of one OpenWebText
                              document (document index 193, 485 words)
  bursts/ordinary.txt         retired v3 substrate. It is third-party prose and
                              is not the authors' work. bursts/provenance.json
                              does not record which document it was cut from,
                              so it is listed here on the conservative reading
                              rather than on a recorded provenance.
  bursts/pos_pool.json        vocabulary pool tabulated from 200 OpenWebText
                              documents

The OpenWebText dataset is distributed under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0
Universal dedication. The underlying documents are web pages written by third
parties, and any rights in them remain with their original authors. Anyone
redistributing or reusing the five files above should rely on the dataset's own
terms and the underlying documents' terms, not on the MIT grant above.

The other burst texts ARE covered by the MIT license, because they are not
corpus-derived:

  bursts/fluent_fabricated.txt   hand-written
  bursts/fluent_attested.txt     hand-written
  bursts/scrambled_false.txt     window-shuffled from fluent_fabricated.txt
  bursts/scrambled_true.txt      window-shuffled from fluent_attested.txt
  bursts/random_chars.txt        generated random ASCII

Per-file provenance, including the generator and SHA-256 of every burst text,
is recorded in bursts/provenance.json.

The OpenWebText corpus itself is not contained in this repository in any form.
See the README for how to obtain it.
